.TH KATZENPOST-STATUS 1 "October 2026" "katzenpost-status 0.0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
katzenpost-status \- generate a Katzenpost network status page
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B katzenpost-status
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B katzenpost-status
reads the configured thin client and directory authority settings, queries the
network status, and writes an HTML report.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config FILE
Path to the thin client TOML configuration file.
.TP
.B --dirauthconf FILE
Path to the directory authority configuration TOML file.
.TP
.B --htmlout FILE
Write the generated HTML to FILE.
.TP
.B --network-name NAME
Set the network name displayed in the report.
.TP
.B --ping, --no-ping
Enable or disable the echo service probe.
.TP
.B --pki-document
Include the full PKI document in the report.
.TP
.B --survey
Run network reachability surveys.
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete option list.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The systemd timer reads site-specific arguments from
.IR /etc/default/katzenpost-status .
The service runs as the locked
.B katzenpost-status
system account.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR systemd.service (5)
